{
  "summary": "This experiment tested multiprofile aggregation (avgpool) on the scvi_n200 RNA encoder, changing only the profile/aggregation axis from the best prior RNA-only result (single-profile scvi_n200, 0.520 acc / 0.498 F1), and achieved a validation accuracy of 0.650 and F1 of 0.628. Because the encoder and modality were held constant, the ~13-point accuracy gain is cleanly attributable to the multiprofile + avgpool aggregation, confirming that combining multiple profiles adds substantial predictive signal beyond what the single-profile scvi_n200 representation captures. It remains uncertain whether more expressive aggregation strategies (e.g., transformer) could yield further gains, whether this multiprofile advantage persists once an image modality is introduced, and how much additional headroom exists above the current ~0.65 accuracy."
}

